        "### Interpretation for Exercise 17\n",
        "\n",
        "1.  **Which method has highest modularity?** &mdash; Louvain typically achieves the highest modularity score among these three methods for the Karate Club graph. In this run, Louvain achieved a modularity of **0.4439**, followed by Greedy Modularity (**0.4110**), and then Label Propagation (**0.3095**). A higher modularity score indicates a better partition, where communities are densely connected internally and sparsely connected externally.\n",
