    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1bab991e4bc51dff"
      },
      "source": [
        "<div style=\"border-left: 5px solid #4B2E83; background-color: #F9F7FC; padding: 20px 25px; margin: 20px 0; border-radius: 5px;\">\n",
        "  <h2 style=\"color: #4B2E83; font-family: 'Encode Sans', 'Arial', sans-serif; margin-top: 0;\">A. Why Interactive Visualization?</h2>\n",
        "  <p style=\"font-size: 1.05em; color: #555; line-height: 1.7;\">\n",
        "    Static matplotlib plots work well for small networks (&lt;100 nodes). For larger networks, interactive tools allow you to:\n",
        "  </p>\n",
        "  <ul style=\"color:#333; line-height:1.8;\">\n",
        "    <li><strong>Zoom and pan</strong> to explore different regions.</li>\n",
        "    <li><strong>Hover</strong> over nodes for details.</li>\n",
        "    <li><strong>Drag</strong> nodes to rearrange the layout.</li>\n",
        "    <li><strong>Filter</strong> by community or metric.</li>\n",
        "    <li><strong>Export</strong> as interactive HTML files.</li>\n",
        "  </ul>\n",
        "  <h3 style=\"color: #32006E;\">Tools</h3>\n",
        "  <ul style=\"color:#333; line-height:1.8;\">\n",
        "    <li><strong>Pyvis:</strong> Simple Python-to-HTML network visualization. Great for quick interactive exploration.</li>\n",
        "    <li><strong>Plotly:</strong> Full-featured plotting library with network support. Good for dashboards.</li>\n",
        "    <li><strong>ipysigma:</strong> Sigma.js wrapper for Jupyter. Handles thousands of nodes efficiently via WebGL.</li>\n",
        "  </ul>\n",
        "</div>"
      ],
      "id": "1bab991e4bc51dff"
    },
    {
